              "value": "Component of the nuclear body, also known as nuclear domain 10, PML oncogenic domain, and KR body (PubMed:8910577). May be involved in the pathogenesis of acute promyelocytic leukemia and viral infection (PubMed:8910577). May play a role in chromatin-mediated regulation of gene expression although it does not bind to histone H3 tails (PubMed:24267382)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION",
          "note": {
            "texts": [
