                    "source": "PubMed"
                  },
                  {
                    "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
                    "id": "8910577",
                    "source": "PubMed"
                  }
                ],
                "value": "Localized to nuclear structures termed LANDS, for LYSp100-associated nuclear domains. LANDS are globular, electron-dense structures most often found in the nucleoplasm, but also found at the nuclear membrane and in the cytoplasm, suggesting that these structures may traffic between the cytoplasm and the nucleus (PubMed:8695863). Also colocalizes with PML in a subset of PML nuclear bodies (PubMed:8910577)"
              }
            ]
          },
